<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Hardened Runtime entitlements for the aios.app main executable (Contents/MacOS/aios) (TODO 951).
  planSigning in scripts/app-shell.mjs applies them only when signing the distributed build with a Developer ID (or with AIOS_HARDENED_RUNTIME=1).
  Starting point is Electron's default (electron-builder's templates/entitlements.mac.plist). For the reasons see
  "Developer ID, Hardened Runtime and notarization" in docs/notes/app-shell.md.

  - allow-jit / allow-unsigned-executable-memory: V8 (main, and the MCP gateway, which runs the same executable with ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE=1).
  - disable-library-validation: the native module main loads (better-sqlite3-multiple-ciphers). In a Developer ID build the .node files are
    signed with the same Team ID, so it should work without this (presumed), but it is needed when trying the Hardened Runtime with a self-signed build (no Team ID).
  - device.audio-input: voice input records through getUserMedia in the renderer. Under the Hardened Runtime, without this entitlement the request is
    denied without showing the microphone prompt. The text TCC shows is NSMicrophoneUsageDescription in Info.plist (infoPlistOps in scripts/app-shell.mjs).
  - automation.apple-events: Apple Events sent by osascript, run by a session's child (a shell), are attributed to TCC's "responsible process"
    = aios.app. Under the Hardened Runtime, without this the Automation prompt is not shown and the request is denied (presumed; VS Code has the same key).
  - allow-dyld-environment-variables is not set (aios does not use DYLD_*. ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE / NODE_OPTIONS are
    environment variables read by Electron / Node, not by dyld; presumed, verify on a real machine).
-->
<plist version="1.0">
  <dict>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.automation.apple-events</key>
    <true/>
  </dict>
</plist>
